// Web search (docs/29 "SearXNG"): a SearXNG the server runs itself, its engines' requests sent through Tor (the ied.tor
// plugin), for the AI's web_search tool and any plugin (websearch.search). Its server code (code/) is compiled into the
// server; its UI module draws Settings > Web > Search.
{
	"manifestVersion": 1,
	"id": "ied.websearch",
	"name": "Web Search",
	"version": "0.1.0",
	"description": "Web search for the AI through a SearXNG IED runs itself, its engines asked through Tor.",
	"publisher": "IED",
	"ied": { "api": "^1" },
	"runtime": { "kind": "builtin", "entry": "WebSearch::Activate", "ui": "ui/index.js" },
	"permissions": ["process.spawn", "net.egress", "ai.tools"],
	"contributes": {
		"settings": { "schema": "settings.schema.json", "page": "Web/Search" },
		"skills": ["skills"],
		"settingsPages": [
			{
				"id": "ied.websearch.search",
				"page": "Web",
				"title": "Search",
				"view": "SearchSettings",
				"keys": ["websearch.engines", "websearch.useTor", "websearch.results", "websearch.safeSearch", "websearch.language", "websearch.timeoutSeconds", "websearch.newCircuitOnBlock", "websearch.stopAfterSeconds", "websearch.instanceUrl", "websearch.python", "websearch.searxngFolder"]
			}
		],
		"bindings": {
			"provides": [
				{ "name": "websearch.search", "version": "1", "kind": "function", "description": "A web search: {query, engines?, count?, page?, time_range?, language?} -> {query, viaTor, text, results: [{title, url, content, engines, published?}], total, answers, suggestions, failed: [[engine, reason]]}" },
				{ "name": "websearch.status", "version": "1", "kind": "function", "description": "{} -> {state, url?, summary?, error?, viaTor, engines, unknownEngines, lastSearch?}" }
			],
			"consumes": [
				{ "name": "websearch.search", "version": "1" },
				{ "name": "tor.proxy", "version": "1", "optional": true },
				{ "name": "tor.newCircuit", "version": "1", "optional": true }
			]
		},
		"systemMessageSections": [
			{ "id": "websearch", "text": "web_search(query) searches the web: results from several engines at once, through a SearXNG on this machine whose requests leave through Tor. Search when the answer lies outside the workspace - current documentation, an error message, a library's API - and say where an answer came from." }
		],
		"toolCalls": [
			{
				"name": "web_search",
				"description": "Search the web: the results of several engines at once (title, URL, snippet, which engines found it, a date when known), through a SearXNG on this machine whose requests leave through Tor. engines narrows it to some of the configured engines (github and stackoverflow for code); time_range keeps recent results; page gives the next ones. Example: web_search(query: \"tokio select! cancellation safety\", engines: [\"github\", \"stackoverflow\"]).",
				"class": "net",
				"group": "web",
				"inputSchema": {
					"type": "object",
					"properties": {
						"query": { "type": "string", "description": "What to search for, as you would type it into a search engine." },
						"engines": { "type": "array", "items": { "type": "string" }, "description": "Only these engines (SearXNG's names, from the configured ones); all configured ones when absent." },
						"count": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 20, "description": "How many results to show (the owner's default when absent)." },
						"page": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 10 },
						"time_range": { "enum": ["day", "week", "month", "year"] },
						"language": { "type": "string", "description": "A language code (en, de, fr-CA); the owner's default when absent." }
					},
					"required": ["query"],
					"additionalProperties": false
				},
				"function": "WebSearch::SearchTool",
				"timeoutSeconds": 180,
				"resultBudgetTokens": 4000
			}
		]
	}
}
